            description='Optional resolved entity id (32-char hex). When set, the embedding attaches\nto exactly this entity, bypassing `(type, key, name)` resolution. This is\nthe identity a managed backfill has for each entity it enumerates from a\nsnapshot — it holds the id but not the original external `key`, which the\nid is a one-way hash of, so name-based resolution would create a phantom\nname-keyed twin instead of attaching to the keyed entity. `entity_id`\ntakes precedence over `key`/`name`; `type` is still resolved for the\nentity record.'
